# Every checkout of this repository holds the same bytes, on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows checks files out with CRLF while the tools that
# generate them write LF. Nothing looks wrong — the code runs, the tests pass —
# right up until something compares a generated file with the one on disk. The
# OpenAPI check did exactly that and failed both Windows jobs in CI with
# "openapi.json is out of date", while the two files were byte-for-byte
# identical apart from thirty-one thousand carriage returns.
#
# A generated artefact that is only correct on one operating system is not a
# generated artefact anybody can check.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated and compared byte for byte — these are the ones the rule exists for.
*.json     text eol=lf
*.mjs      text eol=lf
*.js       text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.css      text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf

# Written by scripts/make-icons.mjs, which emits PNG bytes by hand. Touching a
# newline in one of these corrupts it.
*.png      binary

# Windows launchers only work with CRLF.
*.bat      text eol=crlf
*.cmd      text eol=crlf
